  "semantic_checks": [
    "Forward coordinates are v=x+i*y and vb=x-i*y. Inverse coordinates are x=(v+vb)/2 and y=-i*(v-vb)/2, with both substitution compositions proved identities. v and vb remain independent polynomial variables over C; no conjugacy relation is used.",
    "Homogeneity is preserved by the actual linear inverse substitution. On literal balanced support, d0=d1 together with d0+d1=2m forces the unique monomial v^m*vb^m. Odd homogeneous degree forces empty support and the zero polynomial.",
    "Forward product is literally x^2+y^2. The axis coefficient of (x^2+y^2)^m at x^k is exactly 1 for k=2m and zero otherwise; proved by the actual killCompl axis restriction and its coefficient theorem.",
    "The homogeneous radial coefficient is exactly the original Cartesian coefficient at x^(2m), recovered after descent. No L1-to-coefficient estimate or hidden amplification is asserted.",
    "For an arbitrary finite balanced polynomial, the map d->d0 is injective on the actual support. Thus finite image summation introduces no repeated terms, and the original Cartesian axis coefficient equals the unique balanced coefficient.",
    "m=0, zero coefficient, zero polynomial and empty support are all included. No nonzero polynomial assumption is needed and no division by coefficients occurs."
  ],
